<!--
  Transformer Documentation — ArchitectureOverview
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.transformer.documentation.ArchitectureOverview
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:transformercap="org.blockml.bml.transformer.capability"
  xmlns:transformerdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.transformer.documentation"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow">

  <name>ArchitectureOverview</name>
  <type>transformerdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>Operation-based transformer process and module map</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[
    Entry: transformercap:RunTransformation (Transformer.run). Exclusive
    worktree lock. The orchestrator sequences process steps; it does not
    implement them.

    workflow:ModelOperation is the abstract envelope for one unit of
    work inside a ModelTransformation. Concrete subtypes (today
    workflow:AgenticOperation) are instantiated. Process steps
    (Prepare, executor, Reflect, Persist, Finalize) are not the same as
    ModelOperations. Lifecycle packages of the ModelTransformation live
    under the library-local `_meta.transform` package (pending /
    running / succeeded / failed) and match its status. `_meta` is the
    shared metadata package for the library; it is created when missing.
    Future extensions use other packages under `_meta`.

    The orchestrator writes envelope fields the same way for every
    subtype. A registered transformercap:OperationExecutor does only
    type-specific work. Default: AgenticExecutor for AgenticOperation
    (isolated agent process; output candidate is agent stdout).
    ToolExecutor for ToolOperation (npm CLI via npx).

    [1] Prepare Execution — transformercap:PrepareExecution
        Default: deterministic. Validate the pending contract (status=
        Pending, concrete operations, AgenticOperation requires a Task,
        ToolOperation requires command,
        createdAt; no executionId or start/finish fields on the
        ModelTransformation), require a
        clean Git worktree, assign a unique executionId (type:UUID),
        sequence, startedAt, and baseCommit (HEAD),
        set status=Running, relocate to _meta.transform.running, then commit.
        When template is true, leave the pending Block in place, copy it
        (including SubBlocks / bound T), set template=false on the copy,
        rewrite local type FQNs onto the copy, and relocate that copy
        instead.
        Resolve parameters: parametersSource (CLI --parameters-source
        over pending) closes a pending expression against this Block,
        copies that Property onto parameters, and ignores --parameters.
        Otherwise StructType merges CLI JSON over pending; other types
        replace. Write a value only when one exists.
        Bound T defaults to type:Text. parametersSource faults write
        ParametersException onto exception; operations are skipped.
        If the contract is violated or the worktree is dirty, do not start.

    Then for each ModelOperation, in order:

        Persist operation Running — clean worktree, operation
        status=Running, operation baseCommit=HEAD, commit. Recovery
        boundary: after a crash it is clear which operation started and
        on which commit.

        [2] Operation executor — transformercap:OperationExecutor
            Lookup by the instance type FQN (most specific match).
            Default AgenticExecutor (transformercap:ExecuteTask): close
            the Task instance (all expressions become literals; element
            names are type FQNs). New isolated agent process receives
            only that snippet and executes Task.run. Does not receive
            the AgenticOperation or Running ModelTransformation
            identity. May change BML model source. Returns output text.
            Must not write ModelTransformation metadata (including
            operations) or files under _meta/transform/. Does not
            commit; model changes stay uncommitted until Persist.
            Claude default: Edit(**/*.bml), deny
            Edit(**/_meta/transform/**) and Edit(**/node_modules/**),
            Bash limited to npx blockml.

        [3] Reflect on Execution — transformercap:ReflectOnExecution
            Envelope. Default: deterministic. No agent process. Must
            not change the model. Reads the git trace for changedFiles.
            When the operation's captureOutput is true, writes the
            executor output text onto output. Skipped when the
            executor throws; output never decides Succeeded vs Failed.

        [4] Persist Execution — transformercap:PersistExecution
            Default: deterministic. Writes changedFiles, output, status,
            completedAt, and on failure a BML exception onto this
            ModelOperation. When the executor succeeded, applies this
            operation's resultMappings onto ModelTransformation.result
            before status=Succeeded. A mapping fault writes
            ResultException onto the operation and sets Failed.
            Commits model changes together with the operation terminal
            state. Must not relocate the ModelTransformation. A Failed
            ModelOperation aborts remaining operations.

    [5] Finalize Execution — transformercap:FinalizeExecution
        Default: deterministic. Always runs after a started execution.
        Succeeded only when every ModelOperation succeeded:
        status=Succeeded, completedAt, relocate running to succeeded.
        Otherwise status=Failed, completedAt, relocate running to
        failed. Does not resolve result. Operation exception, including
        ResultException from resultMappings, lives on the failed
        ModelOperation. ParametersException lives on
        ModelTransformation.exception. A ModelOperation failure leaves
        that aggregation empty. Commits after the terminal relocation.

    TypeScript:
    • runtime/transformer.ts → transformercap:RunTransformation
    • pipeline/prepare.ts → transformercap:PrepareExecution
    • executor/agentic-executor.ts → transformercap:AgenticExecutor
    • executor/tool-executor.ts → transformercap:ToolExecutor
    • pipeline/execute.ts → executor dispatch
    • pipeline/reflect.ts → transformercap:ReflectOnExecution
    • pipeline/persist.ts → transformercap:PersistExecution
    • pipeline/finalize.ts → transformercap:FinalizeExecution
  ]]></documentation>

